          "noscript": [],
          "content": "CV\n\nAndrew Dumitru Chincea\n\nContact\nEmail\nachincea@students.kennesaw.edu\nGitHub\ngithub.com/andrewc156\nLinkedIn\nwww.linkedin.com/in/andrewchincea\nEducation\n\nKennesaw State University\nMarietta, GA\n\nB.S. in Mathematics (Statistics concentration); B.S. in Data Science and Analytics\nExpected May 2028\n\nJunior in the 2026–27 academic year.\n\nMathematics\nCalculus I–III, Linear Algebra, Ordinary Differential Equations, Real Analysis, Topology\nStatistics & Data Science\nStatistical Methods I & II, Programming in R, Data Visualization\nComputing\nProgramming and Problem Solving I & II\nResearch interests\n\nAnalytic number theory; topological and graph-based data analysis; statistics and machine learning for scientific data.\n\nPublications and preprints\n\nTsz Ho Chan and Andrew Chincea. Largest kth-Power Divisor of a Random Integer. Submitted.\n\nResearch experience\nUndergraduate Research Assistant – RiverNets (TDA Lab)\nAug 2026 – Present\n\nKennesaw State University · Advisor: Dr. Mehmet Aktas\n\nDeveloped a graph-Laplacian regression model that predicts hourly water quality (water temperature, dissolved oxygen, specific conductance, pH, turbidity) at river stations with no data, using a smoothness penalty along the river network.\nDownloaded, cleaned, and audited hourly USGS continuous water-quality records from 28 Colorado River Basin stations, tracking data completeness by station and variable.\nBuilt river-network graphs in NetworkX from MERIT Hydro 90 m flow directions (67,401 nodes for the Colorado basin, compressed to 67), along with graphs for the Chattahoochee basin.\nApplied Kron (Schur-complement) reduction to collapse the network exactly onto the station nodes, matching the full Laplacia",
